Instance Terminal Correction - Error: CDBOA-611

The error CDBOA-611 was found on the Elpida test case. This error is caused
by having more than one instance terminal on a single terminal on an
instance. This was allowed in Virtuoso before 446 but is not supported in
OpenAccess. This has been fixed in later versions of Virtuoso.

ERROR   (CDBOA-611): Cellview <path> is incomplete because the CDBA version      
                     includes instance terminals with the same name <name>      
                     connected to different nets.
                     
                      Generated 22 times. In releases prior to IC 4.4.6, CDBA   
                     allows instances to have terminals with the same name as   
                     long as these are attached to different nets. OpenAccess   
                     does not. Correct the terminal names in CDBA before        
                     translating these cellviews, either by editing the         
                     cellviews manually or by regenerating them using the latest
                     version of CDBA.

To fix this problem the programs in the file OAfixDupInstTerm.il were
created. These will report and fix any instance which has a terminal with
two instance terminals connected to the same net. If the instance has a
terminal connected to different nets, the program checks the nets to see if
they have more than one connection, if not, one of the instance terminals
is deleted, this was an error in early releases of VXL. If both nets have
more than one connection, the program reports the problem and the user must
manually fix it.
The procedures are run on the CDBA database. You may run them on a library
or cell basis.
OAfixDupInstTermsLib - Processes libraries to correct data causing cdb2oa
error 611.
Arguments:
?log - Open port to add output log information
?logFileName - Name of log file to create. Default is libEdit<PID>.log
?libList - List of libraries or name of library to process. By default all
           the libraries in the cds.lib are processed.
?skipList - Name or list of libraries to skip processing
?viewList - Name or list of views to process

OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "logFile" ?libList "libName" )

      - Processes named library
OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "logFile" ?libList list( lib1 lib2... ) )
      - Processes libraries in list
OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "logFile" )
      - Processes all libraries in cds.lib
OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "logFile" ?skipList list( lib1 lib2... ) )
      - Processes all libraries in cds.lib except those in skip list

OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "DupInstTerms_ether.log3" ?libList "ether" ?viewList "layout" )      
OAfixDupInstTermsLib( ?logFileName "logFile" ?viewList "layout" )

      - Processes the layout views in all libraries in cds.lib,

OAeditCellFixDupInstTerms - Processes named cell and views. Use this if you
only have a few views to fix.
Arguments:
?libName - Name of library for cell - REQUIRED
?cellName - Name of cell to process - REQUIRED
?cellId - ID of a cell in a library - Overrides libName and cellName
?viewList - List of views to process. Default is all views.
?log - Open output log file port. Default is stdout

OAeditCellFixDupInstTerms( ?libName "libName" ?cellName "cellName" ?log stdout )
      - Processes all the views of a cell
OAeditCellFixDupInstTerms( ?libName "libName" ?cellName "cellName" \
      ?viewlist "layout" )
      - Process the layout view from the cell, output to stdout

